OGRE patch (ours): GLES render textures multisample in tile memory with
EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture.

OGRE 14.6's GLES2 multisample render texture is a second framebuffer of multisample renderbuffers,
resolved by glBlitFramebuffer in swapBuffers. On a tile GPU (Mali, Adreno, PowerVR) that writes
every sample to memory before the blit reads them back, several times the bandwidth of the
single-sample target. Where the driver has GL_EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture this patch
attaches the texture itself with glFramebufferTexture2DMultisampleEXT (and gives multisample depth
renderbuffers that extension's storage): the samples live in tile memory and are resolved into the
texture as each tile is written out, never stored. There is no second framebuffer, so swapBuffers
takes the single-sample path (ogre-gles2-discard-depth-on-swap.patch: depth and stencil
invalidated). The sample count is limited by GL_MAX_SAMPLES_EXT. Without the extension OGRE's blit
path is unchanged. The log says which path a multisample framebuffer takes.

diff --git a/RenderSystems/GLES2/include/OgreGLES2FrameBufferObject.h b/RenderSystems/GLES2/include/OgreGLES2FrameBufferObject.h
index 4909614..926783b 100644
--- a/RenderSystems/GLES2/include/OgreGLES2FrameBufferObject.h
+++ b/RenderSystems/GLES2/include/OgreGLES2FrameBufferObject.h
@@ -59,6 +59,8 @@ namespace Ogre {
         
     private:
         void initialise() override;
+        /// Multisampled through EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture (no mMultisampleFB).
+        bool mImplicitMultisample = false;
     };
 
 }
